R36-I — REHEARSAL-FREE INTERFERENCE-AWARE WRITING (nswrite) — s2/lifecycle_bakeoff.py
Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B, RTX 3090, 6 rounds x 40, 2 SEEDS, PYTHONHASHSEED=0, scaffold-shared.
The frontier probe: can new-stream knowledge be written into weights WITHOUT replaying old inputs?
nswrite projects each FIXED trainable Linear's weight-gradient off the null space of old-stream
last-token input activations (per-module low-rank basis U via QR; kept as TRAINING state only, no old
prompts/answers; bias frozen; single dense checkpoint at inference). Controls: naive_fixed (no
projection), nswrite_rand (matched-rank RANDOM basis). ours = growing replay reference.

