RESULT (positive, both seeds consistent: seed0 nswrite all-seen 0.783, seed1 0.792):
1. REHEARSAL-FREE nswrite beats the no-projection floor by +0.30 all-seen (0.792 vs 0.485), with NO
   replay — closing ~40% of the gap from naive (0.485) to replay (0.910).
2. ATTRIBUTABLE to interference-awareness, not gradient shrinkage: the matched-rank RANDOM-basis
   control does nothing (0.490 ≈ naive 0.485), while the activation basis captures 35x the gradient
   energy (occupancy 0.92 vs 0.20) and delivers the entire gain. This is the R23/R31 attribution
   discipline applied to the write mechanism.
3. ZERO plasticity cost: newest_stream_final tied at 0.975 across ALL arms -> nswrite DOMINATES the
   stability-plasticity frontier (higher retention at equal newest), not a stability regularizer trade.
4. SATURATION SIGNAL: occupancy rises 0.74->0.92 over rounds; the forgetting that REMAINS (S0 0.56)
   tracks that saturation -> the first MEASURED signal of interference-free write-subspace saturation,
   i.e. the principled point at which function-preserving GROWTH becomes necessary (phase 2).

HONEST BOUNDS: nswrite (0.792) is still below replay (0.910) -> it does not fully solve rehearsal-free
CL, but it is the first attributable, replay-free, plasticity-preserving reduction of catastrophic
forgetting we've produced, and it comes with a measured growth-necessity trigger. 0.5B synthetic;
2-seed (large, consistent effect). Pod e7syc0y4lqf8w0 terminated.

NEXT (phase 2, per converged codex plan): grow-on-saturation — when occupancy is high AND effective
gradient collapses AND newest learning fails, add capacity; compare DEPTH growth (grow_qwen) vs
WIDTH/parallel-adapter/routed growth at matched compute. If depth doesn't restore write capacity but
width/parallel does, that is the first principled statement of WHAT KIND of growth continual learning
needs (small->large as learned allocation of fresh low-interference write branches, later consolidated).
